=0.03, YE=0.03, PS=0.02\n# iter 2 (less flavors): 0.63\n# iter 3 (more flavors): 0.56 \n# iter 4 (nearly same, 0.18 flav, 0.07 oil, 0.05 MC): 0.63 - worse!\n# \n# Small perturbations caused big changes. iter 4 should be similar to iter 1 but got worse.\n# Maybe the evaluator is noisy, or the specific ratios matter a lot\n# \n# Let me try swapping in different ingredients to see what helps\nprint(\"try different protein sources, add color, try konjac\")\n", "\n# Same recipe as iter 5 gave 0.508 now vs 0.460 before - evaluator is NOISY!\n# Iter 5: 0.460, Iter 11: 0.508, difference ~0.05\n# This means many of my comparisons may be noise. Let me re-check what's actually a real trend.\n# \n# iter 1 (carr, 0.03, no konjac): 0.535\n# iter 5 (konjac 0.03, no carr): 0.460  \n# iter 11 (same as 5): 0.508\n# So konjac vs carrageenan: ~0.48 vs 0.535 \u2014 konjac better (~0.05 improvement)\n# \n# iter 4 (same base but MC=0.05 instead of 0.04, canola=0.07 instead of 0.06, flav=0.18): 0.628\n# Big jump up - probably real that MC increase hurts? or noise?\n# \n# iter 6 (coconut oil swap): 0.70 - much worse, likely real\n# iter 7 (tapioca swap): 0.537 - within noise band\n# iter 10 (added nat veg color, removed PS): 0.71 - much worse, real\n# iter 9 (removed potato starch, bumped konjac): 0.59 - worse, possibly real\n# iter 8 (shifted ratios): 0.59 - worse\n#\n# Best: konjac + carrageenan? Let me try adding BOTH as binders\nprint(\"Try hybrid binder: konjac + carrageenan small\")\n", "\n# Summary of best results:\n# iter 5: 0.460 (base recipe with konjac powder)\n# iter 11: 0.508 (SAME recipe) - so noise ~0.05\n# \n# All other variants: >= 0.51, most worse.\n# \n# Best strategy for remaining 4: stick with the best recipe (iter 5) and try \n# subtle tweaks that might help a bit.\n# Key insight: pea protein > SPC, konjac powder > carrageenan, canola~sunflower, potato starch > tapioca\n# \n# Try: slightly different flavor amount, or try adding plant flavors\n# Or: replace yeast extract with soy sauce\nprint(\"try soy sauce replacement for YE\")\n"]}